{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "זה שמי לעלם", :translit "zeh shmi l'olam", :gloss "This is My name forever"} {:he "זה", :translit "zeh", :gloss "this"} {:he "י\"ב", :translit "y\"b", :gloss "twelve"} {:he "שם של י\"ב אותיות", :translit "shem shel y\"b otiyot", :gloss "a name of twelve letters"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "זה", :b "י\"ב"}], :frame {:text "A divine Name of twelve letters was transmitted to Moses. The Mishnah states that one who articulates the Name by its letters has no share in the World to Come, and those who knew it included the High Priest's deputies. R. Yehudah further taught that a twelve-letter Name was used for preparatory consecration of the High Priest on the Day of Atonement. The connection to the word zeh at Exodus 3:15 anchors this tradition in the verse's declaration of God's eternal name.", :sources ["Mishnah Sanhedrin 10:1" "Kiddushin 71a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "זה", :a-value 12, :b "י\"ב", :b-value 12, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:13:19.616124230Z", :model "glm-5.2"}